Between 1970 and 2010, the city of Sydney was plagued by LGBTIQ bias-motivated violence. At least 30 people were killed — bashed on streets, pushed from cliffs, murdered in their homes. The Sackar Inquiry (2023) was an independent examination of these deaths. The aim of this project is to present the inquiry's findings in a compelling and accessible format: a cross-referenced corpus of the 3,000-page report and other public records.
